   "text": "I disappeared from LinkedIn for around 2 years.\n\nNo posts. No comments. Radio silence.\n\nAnd it wasn't because the posts had stopped working.\n\nAt one point we were generating 10 MQLs a day from posts that took me 30 minutes to write.\n\nThe leads kept coming. Operations didn't keep up.\n\nEvery new client meant the same manual process, run again by hand.\n\nSo I stepped back. No content. No LinkedIn. I spent that time on systems instead.\n\nThen ChatGPT dropped. I'll admit it: I spent over a month wondering how much of what we'd built I'd have to dismantle and start again.\n\nHere's what those two years taught me:\n\n1. Content gets you the lead. A system keeps it.\n2. If a process only works when you run it, it isn't a process yet.\n3. Stepping away is the only honest test of a system.\n\nContent without a foundation is like building a skyscraper on sand.\n\nWhat's the one process in your funnel that still needs you to run it?",
