   "text": "98,000 calendar invites. 1,990 registrations. 321 people live. 25 sales calls.\n\nAll from one session Shweta Jhajharia's team at Growth Idea ran with us in August 2025.\n\nThe numbers don't tell you why. They do tell you where to look. Here's what I'd take from them for your next live event:\n\n1/ Plan the calendar as a channel\n98,000 of the 99,859 people reached got a calendar invite. Give it its own list, its own copy and its own owner, the way you would email.\n\n2/ Registration is a promise. Show-up is the test.\n1,990 registered and 321 came live, about 16%. Spend as much effort on the reminders as on the invite.\n\n3/ Ask for the call while people are in the room\n25 sales calls came from that one session. Put the offer and the booking link inside the session, not in a follow-up a week later.\n\n4/ Fix one number at a time\nAcross all 11 sessions: 80 sales calls. Find the stage that leaks most, fix that one, then run it again.\n\nThat last step is Day 3 of the 3-Day AI RevOps Workshop: an AI agent reads the numbers and flags the leak.\n\nWhich stage of your funnel leaks most?",
